SUMMARY:The 2026 HeART of Portland: K-12 Arts Showcase + Miller Family Free Day
DESCRIPTION:Overview\n\n\n\nWelcome to the HeART of Portland: K-12 Arts Showcase + Miller Family Free Day! Enjoy free admission all day in celebration of youth arts and the community partnership between the Museum and city schools. Make art\, see student performances\, and visit the HeART of Portland K-12 Visual Art Exhibition in the new Silver Family Youth and Community Gallery. Explore PAM’s new Rothko Pavilion and the exhibition David Hockney: Works from the Collection of Jordan D. Schnitzer and His Family Foundation which inspired the HeART of Portland collaborative art project.  \n\n\n\nFree tickets can be reserved online one week in advance and are also available at the door. \n\n\n\nSchedule\n\n\n\n11 am – 3 pmARTMAKING: Windows of Our Future Lana and Chris Finley Studio\, Level 0 Create colorful artwork inspired by the art of David Hockney and the architecture of PAM’s new Mark Rothko Pavilion. Facilitated by Portland Public Schools visual art teachers. \n\n\n\nSHORT FILMS BY STUDENTSStevens Room\, Level 0 See short films by Franklin and Roosevelt High School students. \n\n\n\n12 – 3 pmLook With MeSlow-looking conversations\, focused on one artwork at a time\, facilitated by PAM volunteer guides. Starting every half hour. Look for signs showing specific gallery locations. \n\n\n\n1 pm – 2 pm STUDENT PERFORMANCESMark Rothko Pavilion\, 3rd Floor OverlookEnjoy music and dance performances by Portland students of all ages. \n\n\n\n\nOliver Middle School Jazz Band \n\n\n\nFranklin High School Dancers \n\n\n\nRussell Elementary Choir\n\n\n\nJefferson High School Dancers\n\n\n\nRiverdale Grade School Music\n\n\n\n\nThank you\, Portlanders\, for the Arts Access Fund! The Arts Access Fund provides for elementary arts teachers in the six school districts serving Portland and for expanded access to the arts for all Portlanders. At this free day celebration\, we are thrilled to present student performances from four districts served by the Fund: Centennial\, Parkrose\, Portland Public Schools\, and Riverdale. \n\n\n\nMiller Family Free Days are generously supported by Sharon L. Miller and Family. Additional funding is provided by The Lamb Baldwin Foundation. \n\n\n\nRelated events\n\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Free & discounted\n						 x 											Lectures & talks\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												Look With Me												\n									\n						\n							\n										\n														\n								General accessibility							\n						\n										\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 26\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1219 SW Park Ave \n				\n						\n					\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Exhibitions\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												2026 HeART of Portland: A Portland Public Schools K-12 Arts Showcase Visual Art Exhibition												\n									\n						\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 15\, 2026 – Sep 20\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1219 SW Park Ave \n				\n						\n					\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n			\n							\n		\n		\n		\n		\n			\n							\n											Free & discounted\n						 x 											Partner events\n															\n						\n							\n											\n												2026 HeART of Portland: A Portland Public Schools K-12 Arts Showcase Opening Celebration												\n									\n						\n							\n										\n														\n								General accessibility							\n						\n										\n					\n		\n						\n			\n																	Apr 15\, 2026 \n			\n						\n							\n										1119 SW Park Ave
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/heart-of-portland-miller-free-day/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:Free & discounted
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230423_MIller-Family-Free-Day-April-2023_0105-Unprocessed-JPEG-scaled.jpg
