SUMMARY:The Long Goodbye
DESCRIPTION:The Long Goodbye (1973) Directed by Robert Altman. 1hr 52min. Rated R. \n\n\n\nCatch the neo-noir Robert Altman classic The Long Goodbye (1973) as part of our film series Pretty\, Witty and Gay—in conversation with the David Hockney exhibition. The Long Goodbye is set in sun-drenched 1970’s Los Angeles and follows Detective Philip Marlowe as he tries to help a friend who is accused of murdering his wife. \n\n\n\nWe do not generally provide advisories about subject matter or potentially triggering content in films\, and films exhibited don’t necessarily reflect the views of PAM CUT or the Portland Art Museum. In addition to the synopses\, trailers\, and other links on our website\, further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on sites like Common Sense Media\, IMDb\, and DoesTheDogDie.com.
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/the-long-goodbye/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:PAM CUT @ The Whitsell,Screenings & experiences
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/The-Long-Goodbye.jpg
END:VEVENT
